{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Windows sweep for the subprocess change: two dispatches that included this merge were cancelled by later dispatches, since the concurrency group cancels in-progress runs. Run 44456347985 at ab323f7df0c, which contains 6b88c9dd03a, ran job `sweep (windows)` 135332660982 to the end. It concluded failure: 10 failed, 19,780 passed.\n\nNone of the 10 failures exercise the files this change touched (authorship_resolution, authorship, sshsig, verify_authorship). All of test_verify_identity_reclaim_perf, the sshsig banner tests and the a2c7 tests passed. The failures are:\n- 4 UTF-8 decode failures in the orphaned-process guidance tests (owned by obtuse-phenocryst-verdin's class).\n- 2 SIGKILL-name failures in grounding/test_harness.\n- 1 CRLF failure in test_snapshot_cache.\n- 1 MAX_PATH checkout-index failure in test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.\n- 1 bridge-state PermissionError.\n- 1 failure in test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084::test_a_git_failure_captures_object_store_forensics. That test checks only the file's own `_git`/`_forensics` test helpers, which 035b7371de8 changed today for read-only git objects (charitable-tyrannical-hydra's class).\n\nOn the same run, `sweep (macos, full suite)`, py3.14, py3.14t and py3.15 succeeded."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795066254523126014,"uuid":"d224be50-71ee-4aa3-b4d3-6db093f270d2"}